From: PyDevices usbif
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: let a user C module borrow the OTG controller for
 host duty

Purpose: the esp32 port creates a device-mode USB PHY at boot and holds it
for the lifetime of the firmware. A module that implements USB host on the
same controller has no way to take it: the IDF host library creates its own
host-mode PHY, and the device-mode one must be released first or the
install fails with "selected PHY is in use".

Two functions, mirroring the existing usb_usj_mode() pattern of
reconfiguring the PHY at runtime:

  usb_phy_otg_release()      delete the device-mode PHY, after the caller
                             has quiesced the device stack
  usb_phy_otg_device_mode()  recreate it, handing the controller back

Both are no-ops in a build without such a module, and nothing in the port
calls them, so behaviour is unchanged unless a module asks.

Provenance: written for usbif Phase 2 host bring-up, 2026-08-30.
Upstream-version range: authored against v1.28.0.
Order: independent of 0001-0003; touches only ports/esp32.
Test: with the host engine, usb_host_install() succeeds after the device
stack is deinitialised and the PHY released, and the board returns to
enumerating as a CDC device after the module hands the controller back.

diff --git a/ports/esp32/usb.c b/ports/esp32/usb.c
index bca2305f1..b3b35ba8a 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/usb.c
+++ b/ports/esp32/usb.c
@@ -62,6 +62,24 @@ void usb_usj_mode(void) {
     };
     usb_new_phy(&phy_conf, &phy_hdl);
 }
+
+// Allow an external module to borrow the OTG controller for USB host duty.
+// The device-mode PHY created at boot must be released (after tud_deinit())
+// before a host stack, which creates its own host-mode PHY, can claim the
+// controller -- and restored when the module hands the controller back.
+// Runtime PHY reconfiguration follows the usb_usj_mode() pattern above.
+void usb_phy_otg_release(void) {
+    if (phy_hdl != NULL) {
+        usb_del_phy(phy_hdl);
+        phy_hdl = NULL;
+    }
+}
+
+void usb_phy_otg_device_mode(void) {
+    if (phy_hdl == NULL) {
+        usb_phy_init();
+    }
+}
 #endif
 
 void mp_usbd_port_get_serial_number(char *serial_buf) {
diff --git a/ports/esp32/usb.h b/ports/esp32/usb.h
index 99437266d..f442b35a7 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/usb.h
+++ b/ports/esp32/usb.h
@@ -30,5 +30,7 @@
 
 void usb_phy_init(void);
 void usb_usj_mode(void);
+void usb_phy_otg_release(void);
+void usb_phy_otg_device_mode(void);
 
 #endif // MICROPY_INCLUDED_ESP32_USB_H
